WEBVTT

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.980
Rikudo will win!

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:08.980
At the same time, I will beat
myself and beat you, Kurahara.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.990
What will you show me?

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.260
Kakeru!

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:22.710
King is...

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.800
<i>Tokyo Sport first-year Sakaki Kosuke
puts on a tremendous burst of speed.</i>

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:32.700
<i>He's pulling ahead of Kansei, who passed
their sash before them at Hiratsuka.</i>

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.770
<i>What a striking debut for this rookie.</i>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:40.010
<i>Damn! Damn, damn!</i>

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.030
<i>Damn, damn!</i>

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.020
<i>Damn, damn!</i>

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:57.990
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.410
Have you been at it?

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.380
Looking for a job, I mean.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.380
Does it look like I have been?

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.120
What are you gonna do? 
Join a works team?

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.580
Are you staying in school?

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.330
Then I'll stay, too.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.800
Let's run the Hakone Ekiden next year, too.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.680
King...

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:42.540
I won't be staying in school,

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.480
but I haven't thought about the future, either.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:50.380
Running at the Hakone Ekiden.
It's all I've thought about for a while now.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.930
Of course.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:56.590
If you told me you had a job lined up,

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.200
I'd be pissed.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.310
Section 8 is a hard section.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.100
Even if you're passed, don't let it bother you.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.000
No one's passing me.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.090
The key point is the Yugyoji Temple slope.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:17.090
<b>Yugyoji Temple</b>

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.410
Save as much stamina as you can for there.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.230
Yugyoji, right?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.130
Question for you:

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:21.360
What is Yugyoji Temple's official name?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.790
King.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:24.470
I'll help you look for a job.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.600
What? How?

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:29.360
There's no way you can.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.600
How are you gonna do that? Tell me.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:32.850
<i>King.</i>

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.360
<i>King!</i>

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:38.230
<i>If you can hear me, give me a sign.</i>

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.830
<i>Now breathe deeply
and stretch your shoulders.</i>

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:55.750
<i>Haiji called me in a panic
because you're going too fast.</i>

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.270
<i>I've got a message for you.</i>

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.300
<i>“When we meet in Otemachi,</i>

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.340
<i>tell me the history of Yugyoji Temple.”</i>

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.310
<b><i>Embrace Your Loneliness</i></b>

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.310
<b>Chikusei-so</b>

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.660
The first floor's full.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.950
Take an empty room on the second.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.210
Okay.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.080
We've sure got a lot this year.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:28.790
Huh?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.260
First-years.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:34.260
Some creep with glasses and a guy
who you can't tell what he's thinking.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.920
Can I use the cooking utensils in the kitchen?

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:42.050
You're here?

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.890
You're free to use whatever you want.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:44.840
Okay.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.210
This is the guy who you can't
tell what he's thinking.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:49.890
This guy wants to move in.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.410
Hello. I'm first-year Kiyose Haiji.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:54.560
I'm a literature student.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.520
I'm Sakaguchi Yohei, sociology student.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.010
I'm a first-year.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:01.780
Nice to meet you.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:08.910
You, too.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.780
I don't know how long we'll be able
to live here, but enjoy your stay.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.870
Do you want some tea if I make some?

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.950
<i>A cheerful and fun college life.</i>

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:31.330
<i>I simply chose that place because
I hoped for something like I'd seen on TV.</i>

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.220
<i>But reality was different.</i>

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.190
<i>My college life was uneventful.</i>

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:43.400
<i>It seems like I'll graduate
having done nothing at all.</i>

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:49.000
<i>If I was wrong about anything, it was me.</i>

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.270
<i>I failed to meet my own expectations.</i>

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:58.500
<i>Cowardly and proud, but still wanting
others to show consideration for me.</i>

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.420
<i>I hated that about myself.</i>

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.380
<i>How I acted and how I felt
were completely different.</i>

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.330
<i>He might...</i>

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:19.460
<i>Haiji might accept me.</i>

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:24.260
<i>I was afraid to think that.</i>

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.740
<i>After all,</i>

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:34.610
<i>he doesn't consider me his best friend.</i>

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.080
<i>It's no use.</i>

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:44.020
<i>No matter where I go or who I'm with,
I always feel like the only one out of place.</i>

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:50.240
<i>I try to be sociable, but I don't feel
like I've opened up to anyone.</i>

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.930
<i>I try not to show any weakness.</i>

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.560
<i>I'm the king. Stay away.</i>

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:00.060
<i>But no one will approach me if I'm like that.</i>

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.310
<i>But if I admit I'm lonely, it's over.</i>

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.950
<i>It's too late to change myself now.</i>

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:08.740
Sakaguchi!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.780
You're thirty seconds behind Tokyo Sport!

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.130
Teito's behind you!

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:16.210
<i>That's a good pace.
You re-established your rhythm.</i>

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.620
<i>But...</i>

00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:23.090
<i>...it's different when I'm running.</i>

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:28.060
<i>We don't have a team if anyone's missing.</i>

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:32.950
<i>I feel like something's expected of me.</i>

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.690
<i>We can cast aside our restraint
and pride to support one another.</i>

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:40.930
<i>But while I'm running, I'm always alone.</i>

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:46.400
<i>Released from everything else,
I can face myself.</i>

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:52.410
<i>When I'm running, I don't need to put on an act.</i>

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:58.830
<i>That's right. I'm nobody.</i>

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:04.320
<i>And that nobody is the real me.</i>

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:10.090
<i>You can go faster, Sakaki!</i>

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.870
<i>More, more!</i>

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:17.010
<i>First-year Sakaki swings his arms fervently
as he pursues the runner in front of him.</i>

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.970
<i>It's the fifteen-kilometer mark. This is it.</i>

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.940
I have a second message from Haiji.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:26.840
<i>“Are you ready to buzz in with your answer?”</i>

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:29.900
<i>Haiji.</i>

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.820
<b>Yugyoji Temple Slope</b>

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:37.950
<i>Haiji, Hakone...</i>

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:46.630
<i>...isn't just </i>your<i> dream anymore.</i>

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.550
<i>It's our dream.</i>

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.390
<i>It's a nice dream.</i>

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.900
<i>So nice, I never want to wake up.</i>

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:10.320
<b>Yugyoji Temple Slope
Section 8 5.5km Remaining</b>

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.450
<b>Totsuka Relay Station</b>

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.450
<b>Section 8 > Section 9</b>

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.450
<b>Time Behind 1st</b>

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.450
<b>Boso
Rikudo</b>

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.450
<b>Rikudo/Ueda Fourth-Year >>> Fujioka Fourth-Year</b>

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.950
<i>What's wrong?</i>

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:20.370
<i>Are you feeling timid?</i>

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.580
Not in the slightest.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.640
How are you doing?

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.910
<i>Sorry, but I feel great.</i>

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.920
<i>In recent history, no runner greater
than Fujioka has been seen</i>

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.630
<i>in the college long-distance running scene.</i>

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:35.650
<i>By competing against him,
you'll become even stronger.</i>

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:40.330
Are you saying I can't beat him yet?

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:44.470
We ran together for a year.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:46.850
So I can tell you this:

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:51.600
To me, you are the greatest runner.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.670
<i>Become stronger, Kakeru.</i>

00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.220
Watch me.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:02.770
Watch what you believed in.

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:13.260
Sakaki!

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:16.660
<i>Tokyo Sport's Sakaki
dropped his pace at the end,</i>

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Time Behind 1st
Boso  ------
Rikudo  0:58
Yamato  6:08
Kikui  8:02
Saikyo  8:17
Kitakan  8:30
Manaka  8:41
Do  9:09
Yokohama  9:34
Kofu  10:42
Top 10 Seeded Schools
Ake  10:52
Tokyo Sport  10:59</b>

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Tokyo Sport/Sakaki First-Year >>> Yasunaga Fourth-Year</b>

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:18.840
<i>but perseveres to pass 
along his team's sash.</i>

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:29.370
See you somewhere on the course.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.320
I didn't think we'd actually meet.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.940
But I'll never acknowledge it.

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:41.510
Kansei has no future.

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:46.120
I just want to pass on our sash.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:49.080
They're all waiting.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:52.980
Sakaki, you did it!

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.340
You placed fifth in your section! Fifth!

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.460
<i>To the line, Kansei!</i>

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.450
<i>Get to the relay line!</i>

00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:59.420
You did it!

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:11.750
Joji.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:15.940
What does it feel like to fall in love?

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:17.230
What?

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.100
It's nice, isn't it?

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.080
I'm in love, too.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:27.560
What? With who?

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:29.540
King!

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:44.850
We're counting on you.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:46.400
I know.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.310
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:54.150
Hey, who is it?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:01.070
Who?!

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:09.410
<b>Section 9</b>

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:09.410
<b>Car 2</b>

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:09.410
<b>Rikudo/Fujioka Kazuma Fourth-Year</b>

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:09.410
<i>Rikudo's Fujioka completes
his first kilometer in 2:48.</i>

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:15.420
<b>Section 9</b>

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:15.420
<b>Car 1</b>

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:15.420
<b>Boso/Sawachi Kosuke Third-Year</b>

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:12.610
<i>Boso's Sawachi runs a 2:46.</i>

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:15.420
<i>Sawachi is speeding ahead. 
He's running.</i>

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.900
<i>They'll be crossing the five-
kilometer mark shortly.</i>

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:28.350
<b>Section 9</b>

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:28.350
<b>Car 2</b>

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:28.350
<b>Kita Kanto/Higure Daiki Third-Year</b>

00:12:23.150 --> 00:12:27.340
<i>Kita Kanto's Higure sprints
to finish his first kilometer in 2:45.</i>

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:30.780
<i>He's closing in 
on Saikyo and Kikui.</i>

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>Section 9</b>

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>Car 3</b>

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>Dochido/Takizawa Tomonori Fourth-Year</b>

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:37.770
<i>Dochido, Yokohama,
and Tokyo Sport,</i>

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.040
<i>which climbed the rankings 
during Section 8,</i>

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:43.000
<i>are racing for a
seeded spot next year.</i>

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.190
<i>Let's check in on 
the motorcycle cam next.</i>

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:51.790
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.070
You can do it!

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:03.310
You can do it!

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:05.720
<i>It's snowing...</i>

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.370
You can do it!

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:19.500
You can do it!

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:27.930
<i>I don't feel anything.</i>

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.120
<i>Am I slow?</i>

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:36.280
<i>All those people...</i>

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.850
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.540
<i>Am I being filmed?</i>

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.960
<i>Does that mean I'm running at a good pace?</i>

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.100
<i>I'm running on the ground, right?</i>

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.780
<b>Running Towards Tomorrow</b>

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.150
<i>What incredible speed!</i>

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.260
<i>Currently running in 13th place
is Kansei's Kurahara Kakeru.</i>

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:11.740
<b>Section 9</b>

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:11.740
<b>Car 4</b>

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:11.740
<b>Kansei/Kurahara Kakeru First-Year</b>

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:11.740
<i>His first kilometer time
is an unbelievable 2:42.</i>

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:14.270
<i>The first three kilometers are all downhill.</i>

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:15.700
<i>It's easy to go fast.</i>

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.160
<b>Section 9</b>

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.160
<b>Car 4</b>

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.160
<b>Kansei/Kurahara Kakeru First-Year</b>

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:19.610
<i>I'm worried he'll throw off 
his own rhythm by running too fast.</i>

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.480
It's beautiful.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.590
Seeing this makes me hate running.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.630
My efforts feel futile.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:33.130
Arrogance is thinking hard work
can solve everything.

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:40.680
But there's more than one goal to aim for.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:45.480
<b>Section 9</b>

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:45.480
<b>Car 4</b>

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:45.480
<b>Kansei/Kurahara Kakeru First-Year</b>

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:45.140
Everyone is equal here. 
We're all even.

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:50.780
We all run the same path,
but we arrive at different finish lines.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.690
I hope you're right.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:58.930
He's almost at five kilometers.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:00.080
Any message?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:02.190
<i>Should I tell him anything?</i>

00:15:02.190 --> 00:15:03.460
I have nothing to tell him.

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:09.930
It's as if he's trying to reach
another dimension by running.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:13.380
I can't interfere with that.

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:17.850
No one must touch Kakeru.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.310
<b>Tokaido Line</b>

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:26.730
He ran Gontazaka in 2:50.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.310
He's a monster.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:30.210
I know because I ran it.

00:15:30.210 --> 00:15:33.030
No one can keep that up until the end.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.720
He's still got more than 15 kilometers to go.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:39.290
Can he not hear the landlord?

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:43.000
I think Haiji's letting him do it.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.120
Hurry, King!

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.550
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:50.550
Kakeru's so fast, we're not gonna make it!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.510
<b>Section 9</b>

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.510
<b>Car 4</b>

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.510
<b>Kansei/Kurahara Kakeru First-Year</b>

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.510
Show some consideration 
for your seniors!

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:03.560
<i>I love these sights.</i>

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:04.060
<b>You Can Do It</b>

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:05.850
<i>It feels like Hakone.</i>

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:10.940
<i>Is the wind keeping the snow from piling up?</i>

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:12.900
<i>Right.</i>

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.880
<i>I have to stay calm today.</i>

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.580
<i>I feel light.</i>

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:24.070
<i>I need to go faster.</i>

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:28.400
<i>There they are.</i>

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:29.740
<i>They're right there.</i>

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.880
<b>Section 9</b>

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.880
<b>Car 4</b>

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:37.350
<i>Kansei's Kurahara instantly passes
Akebono and Kofu Academy.</i>

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:42.260
<i>He just pulled ahead of Tokyo
Sport. He's pulled ahead.</i>

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.480
<i>He's overtaking everyone.</i>

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.690
<i>That probably puts me in tenth.</i>

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.400
<i>I've got about 13 kilometers left.</i>

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:58.750
<i>Since Section 10 is 23 kilometers,
that's 36 all together.</i>

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.120
<i>It's too short.</i>

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:05.780
<i>I could pass everyone
if I kept running like this.</i>

00:17:07.660 --> 00:17:09.170
<i>Keep running?</i>

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.130
<i>Alone, forever?</i>

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:35.990
What will you show me?

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.390
<b>Section 9</b>

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.390
<b>Car 2</b>

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.390
<b>Rikudo/Fujioka Kazuma Fourth-Year</b>

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:02.520
<i>Rikudo's Fujioka has finally
caught up to Boso's Sawachi.</i>

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:11.770
<b>Section 9</b>

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:11.770
<b>Car 1</b>

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.360
<i>He passed him. He passed him instantly.</i>

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.390
<b>1st Boso/Sawachi Kosuke Fourth-Year
2nd Rikudo/Fujioka Kazuma Fourth-Year</b>

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:10.320
<i>Reigning champions Rikudo finally
make their comeback in Section 9.</i>

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.730
<b>No watching the Hakone Ekiden 
from the pedestrian bridge</b>

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.730
<b>Section 10
Expected Time
12:17</b>

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:16.970
Kakeru's crazy, but so is he.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.640
They could do it because they're Rikudo.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:22.390
Each man passed along the sash

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.660
<b>Section 9</b>

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.660
<b>Car 1</b>

00:18:22.390 --> 00:18:24.660
and trusted Fujioka to make a comeback.

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:28.460
It's not something he could've done alone.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:34.440
But when I think of the guys riding on
Fujioka's shoulders, it makes me tremble.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.330
They must've been under incredible pressure.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.540
Boso's Sawachi is falling behind.

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.550
<b>Section 9</b>

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.550
<b>Car 1</b>

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.720
He can't keep up with Fujioka.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:45.640
He's trying to break the section record.

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:47.130
Of course he is.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:50.450
Helping his team win isn't
enough to satisfy him.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:55.690
The man who wants
to pile victory upon victory.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:19:01.110
In all respects, he is undoubtedly
the current champion.

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:02.120
Current?

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.030
That's what you said.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.460
I can't ignore that.

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.160
<i>I can catch up.</i>

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:21.040
<i>No, I'll pass them.</i>

00:19:21.040 --> 00:19:22.840
<i>I'm already ahead of them.</i>

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:26.160
<i>The real me.</i>

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.980
Kurahara! Kurahara!

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:50.500
Rikudo's Fujioka might
break the section record!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.750
He could break the section record!

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.680
<i>I'm sure he will.</i>

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.960
He's inhuman.

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:07.340
<i>I don't care about my apparent position.</i>

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.550
<i>The real problem is my time.</i>

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:12.000
<i>What's happening?</i>

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.030
<i>My field of vision is too broad.</i>

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.810
<i>I can't focus.</i>

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.410
<i>I feel like I've slowed down again.</i>

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:20.740
<i>How are my legs?</i>

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:24.700
<i>My body? My heart? My lungs?</i>

00:20:25.460 --> 00:20:26.960
<i>I can go faster.</i>

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:28.490
<i>I can keep going.</i>

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:29.670
<i>I can keep running.</i>

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.660
<i>Accelerate.</i>

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:34.160
<i>You won't beat me!</i>

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:45.670
<b>Final episode: In The Wind</b>

00:22:40.550 --> 00:22:43.740
Final episode, “In The Wind.”
